{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Difficult Relationships"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Man's Best Friend"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le08ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Perfect Modals - Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Let's review the Perfect Modals - verbs you use to add the meaning of certainty, uncertainty, past possibility and regret."}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <span class=\"strong\">must have done</span> = you are almost sure something happened in the past <ul><li> <span class=\"italic\">Jeff didn't answer the phone when I called him. He must have gone out.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <span class=\"strong\">can't have done</span> = you are almost sure something did not happen in the past  <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">They can't have woken up early. They wanted to sleep in.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <span class=\"strong\">may</span> /  <span class=\"strong\">might</span> /  <span class=\"strong\">could have done</span> = it is possible that something happened in the past but you aren't sure  <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Kevin hasn't arrived yet. He may/might/could have missed the train.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <span class=\"strong\">could have done</span> = you had the ability to do something in the past but did not do it <ul><li><span class=\"italic\"> You could have told us about the new job!</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">should have</span> /  <span class=\"strong\">ought to have done</span> = it was the right thing to do but you didn't do it OR you expected something to happen but it didn't <ul><li><span class=\"italic\"> I should have told you the truth.</li><li><span class=\"italic\"> I ought to have received the money by now.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <span class=\"strong\">would have done</span> = you wanted to do something but you didn't do it in the end <ul><li><span class=\"italic\"> They would have emailed you but the Internet was down yesterday.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "She's used to getting her breakfast at exactly that time every day, and she would have thought that this particular Friday was no exception."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I should have known Coco wouldn't want to do the same."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I always think that she can't possibly have heard anything, but her doggy sense is far more powerful than my human ears. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " State Verbs and Performative Verbs - Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "State Verbs are verbs that talk about a state rather than an action.  <br/>Performative verbs are verbs which perform the action they describe. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " Look at the chart for a summary of how and when to use these specific verbs:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Kind of Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning/Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"State\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Use the Present Continuous tense with some state verbs to emphasize that a situation is temporary for a period of time around the present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"   <span class=\\\"italic\\\">attract</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">like</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">look</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">love</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">sound</span><br/><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The kids <span class=\\\"strong\\\">love</span> having Grandma here.<br/> The kids <span class=\\\"strong\\\">are loving</span> having Grandma here.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Mental State \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Use with the Present Continuous to emphasize that you have recently started to think about something or that you are not sure about something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">find</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">realize</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">regret</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">think</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">understand</span><br/><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">regret</span> that the company is to be folded. </span>(I regret the decision and I'm sorry about it)<br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m regretting</span> my decision to hire him.</span> (I'm increasingly aware that this was the wrong decision)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Performative Verbs \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use these verbs in the Simple Present tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">suggest</span>,   <span class=\\\"italic\\\">acknowledge</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">admit</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">advise</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">apologize</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">beg</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">confess</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">congratulate</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">declare</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">deny</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">forbid</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">guarantee</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">name</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">order</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">permit</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">predict</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">promise</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">refuse</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">remind</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">request</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">thank</span>,  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">warn<br/><br/>  I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">suggest</span> you take the bus today.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I confess that I have a bit of a bias, but I think they are among the most intelligent animals."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She loves having company."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She instantly realized that she had made a mistake and ran off."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She regretted that she had to spend an hour in her cage."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bright"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "intelligent"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: First, like humans, dogs are bright and resourceful. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le08ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words to review. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "resourceful"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having the ability to find quick and clever ways to overcome difficulties"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dogs can be very resourceful at getti