 time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}}], "id": 10}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "engenn11le08ob11re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nMake a Venn diagram. \n"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 11}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn11le08ob11re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "Let me just start by saying that I know humans and dogs are different. Really, I do. But there are a few ways in which our personality traits are actually quite similar to those of our canine friends.<br/>\nFirst, like humans, dogs are bright and resourceful. Take my dog Coco for example. Last Friday she prevented me from sleeping in by scratching on my bedroom door at 6:00 a.m. She's used to getting her breakfast at exactly that time every day, and she would have thought that this particular Friday was no exception. The problem was that it was Easter Friday, a holiday, and I was looking forward to getting a bit of extra rest. I should have known Coco wouldn't want to do the same. Eventually she got tired of waiting, went into the kitchen, opened a bag of Doritos with her paw and gobbled up the entire thing. I confess that I have a bit of a bias, but I think they are among the most intelligent animals.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn11le08ob11re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "59900", "text": "Second, dogs are intuitive. Coco always barks at least ten seconds before I hear anyone at the door. I always think that she can't possibly have heard anything, but her doggy sense is far more powerful than my human ears. <br/>\nThird, canines are kindhearted and personable. She loves having company. Just last week, my brother visited, and Coco must have brought out every single one of her toys and set them at his feet. She wanted to share her most valuable treasures with him. Of course, she also insisted on his scratching her belly in return for her generosity.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn11le08ob11re2img02.jpg"}, {"time": "100000", "text": "Finally, dogs can be cheeky and disobedient. Last week, as I was eating burgers for dinner, she jumped up and grabbed one right off my plate. She instantly realized that she had made a mistake and ran off. She regretted that she had to spend an hour in her cage, surely, but for her the punishment was worth the crime.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn11le08ob11re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le08ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le08ob11re2img01.jpg"}}], "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": []}]}]}